node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.log
dist-single/
test-results/

# Captures are large and machine-local, so the directory contents are ignored — but the
# critic's verdicts are the record of what bar this build was held to, and they were being
# discarded along with them. Rounds 1-3's judgements are already gone this way. Keep the
# JSON; leave the PNGs out. (Ignore the contents, not the directory: git cannot un-ignore a
# file inside an ignored directory.)
shots/*
!shots/review-*.json
# Same reasoning for the interaction rig: the report carries the verdicts, the numbers each
# was measured against, and the apparatus self-check, in 40 KB. The per-scenario traces under
# shots/interaction-<tag>/ are 2 MB of raw per-frame columns and stay out — tools/interaction-score.mjs
# needs them to re-derive a verdict, so re-run the rig rather than expecting them to survive.
!shots/interaction-*.json
